From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:11:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] coherent pages on the census's KVM-only
 view

Under REIMS_VGPU_COHERENT=1 the library owns tracked pages' states: held,
armed, open, frozen. Faults reach it through ops, QEMU's own RAM accesses
through census_coherent_access. An arm drops the mapping before the write
protection, so a page POISON refuses may be written, and goes back held and
to the library rather than being skipped. Marks read line by line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
