  * A failure must never take the VM with it: an -EFAULT nothing answers disarms the whole census
  * (census_fuse) before it is allowed to reach QEMU's fatal path.
  *
+ * Under REIMS_VGPU_COHERENT=1 the same view and markers serve metal2vulkan's trap-coherent
+ * surfaces (shadow_lazy.rs and shadow_coherent.rs there), and nothing is sampled. The library then
+ * owns every tracked page's state, and moves it only under its surface's lock:
+ *
+ *   held    Write-protected: pages and image agree. Reads pass; a write opens the page.
+ *   armed   Poison: the image is ahead of the page. Any access stops in census_on_sigbus, which
+ *           asks the library to sync (ops.fault) and reruns the instruction.
+ *   open    No marker: the guest's CPU may have written, and the image is stale here.
+ *   frozen  Poison over an open page, while a sync merges into it.
+ *
+ * A write to a held page gives a bare -EFAULT. Where the vCPU has just trapped on the page, the
+ * pending page names it. Where it has not, ops.probe arms every held page, nothing having changed
+ * in them, and the rerun's SIGBUS gives the exact address: so a write always has its page.
+ * ARMED -> HELD drops the poison and then write-protects, and POISON and WP cannot swap in one
+ * step, so a vCPU can reach the page between them: census_coh_hold reads pagemap afterwards, and
+ * reports a page that came in meanwhile as written, for a copy in of it. QEMU's own accesses (a
+ * device's DMA, KVM's emulator through an MMIO exit) use the main mapping and raise no fault, so
+ * address_space_map and the direct RAM paths call census_coherent_access.
+ *
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
  */
 
